      "date": "after 1906",
      "kind": "site history",
      "description": "Possibly a 1906 earthquake refugee cottage, one of four such candidates in the Town Center. Refugees hauled the temporary Red Cross shacks out to cheap lots in the outlying districts and weatherproofed, enlarged and re-fenestrated them, leaving the footprint and gable-roof profile as the only surface clues; confirming one takes physical investigation, which has not been done here.",
